inkling2-mini-rdna3

This repository contains code from the following projects.

1. maya-inkling-mini (Project Maya fork with the maya-ik2 engine for Inkling 2 Mini)
   https://github.com/alesha-pro/maya-inkling-mini, commit c520fd14de3b21d67ddc6b7e7348b761aad26d52
   (Project Maya v1.1.70 with the Inkling 2 Mini engine)
   Copyright (c) 2026 Peasant Smith and the Project Maya contributors
   Copyright (c) 2026 Niko1221 and the Strata contributors
   MIT License, see LICENSE.
   Used: src/ik2/* except ik2_rdna.inc and ik2_hip.cuh (the engine: model arithmetic, GGUF loading, resident token
   path, prompt path, drafter support, CPU helpers), include/strata/artifact/gguf_reader.hpp and
   include/strata/hip_compat/*. Modified here for HIP on Windows, the UD-IQ4_XS weight formats and AMD kernels;
   changes are marked "(AMD port)" in the source.
   Not included, used at run time by serve.ps1: serve/ (the chat server), tools/strata_tokenizer.py and
   tools/ik2/chat_template.jinja.

2. Project Maya v1.1.74
   https://github.com/mw00/project-maya (release v1.1.74)
   Copyright (c) 2026 Peasant Smith and the Project Maya contributors; MIT License.
   Used: include/strata/kernels/rdna_wmma.hpp (unchanged), and the first version of src/ik2/ik2_rdna.inc: the grouped
   prompt experts in 32-row tiles (experts_rdna_kernel, experts_rdna_gu, experts_rdna_down, moe_rows_combine), the
   prompt flash attention (attn_flash_rdna), gemm_bf16_cols and rdna_wmma_gpu. This repository extends that file
   (larger tiles, more weight formats, dense products, loop gates, relative bias, decode attention).

3. Strata (through Project Maya)
   https://github.com/Niko1221/Strata
   Copyright (c) 2026 Niko1221 and the Strata contributors; MIT License.
   The include/strata/ headers originate in Strata.

4. Inkling 2 Mini CIRU Halo Agent (gfx1151), version 1.5.0
   https://github.com/ciru-ai/Inkling-2-Mini-CIRU-Halo-Agent-gfx1151
   Copyright 2026 Ciru (source headers: Copyright (c) 2026 CIRU AI)
   Apache License, Version 2.0, see LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt.
   No code was copied. These kernels in src/ik2/ik2_rdna.inc follow designs from its HIP sources and are marked there:
   - hip_moe_prefill.hip: expert tiles of 128 rows and of 256 weight columns, and skipping fragments past a tile's rows
     (experts_rdna128_kernel, experts_rdna256_kernel);
   - hip_glue_prefill.hip: the loop gate's up products and blend in one launch without intermediate matrices
     (loop_gate_up_rdna);
   - hip_attn_prefill.hip: prompt attention with one lane per query and the swapped products S^T = K Q^T, O^T = V^T P^T
     (attn_flash2_rdna_kernel, IK2_FLASH2).
   They were rewritten for this engine's data layouts, weight formats, FP16 arithmetic and Windows. No weights, fitted
   files or other material of that project are included or used.
   From that project's NOTICE: "Ciru's AMD runtime changes, fitted weight files and packaging are distributed under the
   Apache License, Version 2.0."

Used for testing only, not included:
- llama.cpp (https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp, MIT): its greedy output is the reference of scripts/gate.py and
  scripts/reference.json.
- AMD ROCm SDK 7.14.1 Python packages (https://repo.amd.com/rocm/whl-multi-arch): compiler, HIP runtime, hipBLAS.

Model, not included:
- Inkling 2 Mini by Thinking Machines Lab, Apache License 2.0, https://huggingface.co/thinkingmachines/Inkling-2-Mini
- GGUF conversion by Unsloth, https://huggingface.co/unsloth/Inkling-2-Mini-GGUF
  (Inkling-2-Mini-UD-IQ4_XS.gguf at revision ae9327c5fbc7333116ba32eee78bb5d2bbefae4f)
- scripts/reference.json holds token ids and log-probabilities that llama.cpp produced from that model.
